// Ingredient matrix — ALL THREE individually necessary:
//   scrutinee call's body map::len(map::filter(..)) -> const  agree
//   untaken arm's `v65 != u8:2` -> `false` .................. agree
//   guard reads v17 directly (no second ref) ................ agree
//
// Mechanism (probed + CLIF + GXDBG_DYNC): the v17 select fuses whole
// with the map-HOF callee cross-kernel inside it. On the ref-write's
// propagation cycle the region is invoked (v65 fired — consumed ONLY
// by the const-false-guarded arm); the interp's CallSite would not
// even dispatch (any-arg-fired gate), but the kernel calls the callee
// unconditionally, and the callee's interior scaffold-loop DynCalls
// sit at UNCLAIMED key-0 sites which deliver args FIRED by design
// (emit/call.rs "UNCLAIMED scaffold-loop sites keep FIRED delivery",
// the aug08a shared-cache rationale). The fired callback dispatches
// make the SlotFlags word claim a slot fired, the loop fires, the
// callee returns a FIRED disc, the select's organic merge folds
// scrutinee-FIRED, and v17 re-fires; the second ref turns that into a
// guard delivery and the final select echoes at offset 3.
//
// Not a semantics question — the interp's quiet is correct (untaken
// arm's input is not consumed). Fix = the already-designed DynCall
// site-identity v2: per-position CLAIMED sites in scaffold loops
// taking the honest stale mask (CLAUDE.md: scaffold-loop sites are
// "v1, keeping the init-mask approximation"). Emission work, not a
// one-liner. Reduced witness:
{let v41 = u8:100; let v42 = true; let v8 = |v34: bool, v35: i64, v27: f64| -> i64 map::len(map::filter({"k1" => null, "k2" => null}, |kv| str::len(kv.0) > i64:1)); let v60 = &v41; *v60 <- u8:1; let v65 = *v60; let v17 = select v8(v42, i64:0, f64:0.) {v27 if (i32:-1 > i32:42) => v65 != u8:2, _ => v42}; let v79 = &v17; select v65 {u8:100 if *v79 => i64:7, _ => true}}
